}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-12-25.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="015457"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#015457" label="[01:54:57]">&lt;sam_&gt;</a></span><span class="message">[16:14] &lt;mid-kid&gt; Trying to update the gentoo bootstrap, building gcc:14 using the supplied gcc:13 isn't going so well</span></div><div class="line" id="015500"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#015500" label="[01:55:00]">&lt;sam_&gt;</a></span><span class="message">what went wrong exactly?</span></div><div class="line" id="070041"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#070041" label="[07:00:41]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">merry christmas :)</span></div><div class="line" id="135444"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#135444" label="[13:54:44]">&lt;mid-kid&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Googulator: merry christmas!</span></div><div class="line" id="135530"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#135530" label="[13:55:30]">&lt;mid-kid&gt;</a></span><span class="message">#/usr/lib/i386-unknown-linux-musl/gcc/i386-unknown-linux-musl/13.1.0/../../../../../i386-unknown-linux-musl/bin/ld: ../libbacktrace/.libs/libbacktrace.a(state.o): warning: relocation in read-only section `.text'</span></div><div class="line" id="135532"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#135532" label="[13:55:32]">&lt;mid-kid&gt;</a></span><span class="message">#/usr/lib/i386-unknown-linux-musl/gcc/i386-unknown-linux-musl/13.1.0/../../../../../i386-unknown-linux-musl/bin/ld: read-only segment has dynamic relocations</span></div><div class="line" id="135534"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#135534" label="[13:55:34]">&lt;mid-kid&gt;</a></span><span class="message">#collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status</span></div><div class="line" id="135536"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href=